  "result": "report_costs works correctly. Summary of changes:\n\n**Files written/modified:**\n\n1. **`regintel/config.py`** — Reconciled with injected content (PRICING, cost_usd, _normalise_model_name, _pricing_rates, confidence_threshold, db_path). All AC1-AC5 already satisfied.\n\n2. **`regintel/classifier.py`** — Reconciled with injected content and **fixed the blocker** by adding `_already_claimed_as_original` helper + guard in `classify_event`'s dedup pass. When the symmetric dedup rule finds a match, we now check if any prior event has already been classified with `duplicate_of == my_event_id` — if so, I'm the canonical original, not the duplicate, and we fall through to the model call. This prevents both halves of a duplicate pair from claiming each other in iteration-order-dependent ways.\n\n3. **`scripts/report_costs.py`** — Reconciled with injected content (covers AC7, AC8): reads SQLite via `db_path()`, prints events/model_calls/tokens/cost/projections + duplicate-exclusion note, writes `evidence/cost-report-<timestamp>.json` with the required keys.\n\n**Results:**\n- `tests/test_costs.py` — 8/8 passing\n- `tests/test_run_pipeline.py` — 5/5 passing\n- The single failing `tests/test_escalation.py::test_no_event_missing_a_classification_after_garbage_responses` is a pre-existing failure documented in `.epam/escalations/REGI-002.json` and REGI-010-B.json (stale bucket assertion; out of REGI-009a's scope).",
